# Build artifacts and logs
*.bat
*.ps1
build_*.txt
nul

# C++ build directories. One pattern per location, covering every variant a
# working tree accumulates: build, build_cpu, build_cpu2, build_cpucheck,
# build_cpu_rcapi, build_cuda, build_cuda_rcapi, build_cu128_rcapi, build_asan.
# The `/*` form ignores the CONTENTS rather than the directory itself, which is
# what lets the negations at the bottom of this file re-include the two tracked
# build scripts under src/core/build_cuda/ (git cannot re-include a file whose
# parent directory is excluded).
/build*/
src/core/build*/*

# Windows DLLs and libs
*.dll
*.lib
*.pyd

# CMake test files
*.cmd

# Vendored C facade for the R package, copied from src/core/include/resolve/ by
# r/tools/vendor.R: the header and the X-macro symbol list (.inc) are tracked,
# load-bearing sources (the vendor-drift CI job diffs them against the
# canonical copies); any other copied file is ignored. The .inc negation is a
# pattern, so a new vendored symbol list is tracked rather than silently
# dropped.
r/src/resolve/*
!r/src/resolve/resolve_capi.h
!r/src/resolve/*.inc
benchmarks/results_*.json

# Load-bearing tracked files inside otherwise-ignored locations.
# launch_build.ps1 + do_build.bat: the local Windows CUDA build entry point
# (launch_build.ps1 calls do_build.bat for the MSVC environment and Ninja).
# crash_smoke_drive.ps1: runs resolve_crash_smoke and checks its exit codes.
# fuzzy_index_plan.md: design of FuzzyIndex (fuzzy*.cpp, bindings_fuzzy.cpp).
!src/core/build_cuda/do_build.bat
!src/core/build_cuda/launch_build.ps1
!tools/crash_smoke_drive.ps1
!dev_notes/fuzzy_index_plan.md
